    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28119" root="عجر" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَجِرٌ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَجُرٌ</span></b> , applied to a <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وَظِيف</span> [or shank
of a beast], (S, O, K,) <i>Thick;</i> (S, O;) as also
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْجَرُ</span></b> : (O:) or <i>hard,</i> (K, * TA,) <i>and strong;</i>
and in like manner applied to a solid hoof, and
to a pastern. (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And for another meaning of the first of the words, see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَعْجَرُ</span>.

